## Evidence

<!--
Mandatory anti-hallucination gate. Schema/constraint snippets MUST be
copied verbatim from real DDL/migrations — otherwise DEV ports wrong
types/indexes and corrupts prod.
-->

- **Overall status**: `verified` | `estimated` | `mixed` *(pick one)*
- **Source repo**: `<path or URL>` — `<sha or tag>` [verified|estimated]
- **DDL source**: `<e.g. alembic/versions/, db/schema.sql, prisma/schema.prisma>` [verified|estimated]
- **Schema extraction method**: `<e.g. pg_dump --schema-only, prisma db pull>` [verified|estimated]

### Evidence rules

- DDL snippets in `### 2.x` MUST be copied verbatim from a migration file or live dump.
- Every `Source: file:line` field MUST be tagged `[verified]` or `[estimated]`.
- Index/constraint blocks MUST list `CREATE INDEX` / `ADD CONSTRAINT` verbatim (no paraphrase).
- If 0% of references are tagged, the schema is fictional — re-extract from DB.

## Como usar este documento

- **Audience**: dev portando schema para outro DB engine ou desenhando migrations em host alvo.
- **Next action**: ler `## 2. Model details` seção por seção, conferir DDL com `pg_dump` ou similar no alvo.
- **Quando re-verificar**: após qualquer migration nova no sistema alvo ou mudança de engine (postgres → mysql).

